## Purpose

Implement the first Madar v0.3 collaboration slice: append-only case comments for users who already have access to the parent case, with SQL persistence, bounded audit metadata, API, Arabic Blazor UI, and SQL end-to-end verification.

Closes #78.

## Implemented behavior

- Madar-owned `CaseComment` model with bounded plain-text body, author, case, created time, and SQL Server rowversion;
- body is trimmed, required, and bounded to 1..2000 characters;
- case visibility is reused as the comment list/add authorization boundary: creator, current assignee, or `madar.cases.read-all`;
- inaccessible/missing parent cases use the existing not-found masking behavior;
- append-only first slice: no edit/delete/versioning policy is invented prematurely;
- `GET /api/cases/{caseId}/comments` and `POST /api/cases/{caseId}/comments` require authentication; POST also uses the existing anti-CSRF filter and write rate limit;
- comments persist in product-owned `madar.CaseComments` with deterministic `(CaseId, CreatedUtc, Id)` read ordering and EF migration/snapshot coverage;
- `madar.case.comment-added` audit records bounded metadata such as `commentId`; comment body is intentionally excluded from audit attributes/log diagnostics;
- typed Blazor API client and Arabic comments panel are integrated into `/cases/{CaseId:guid}` without a new route;
- comments remain readable after case resolution/closure as append-only collaboration history;
- no reusable `FoundationKit.Comments`/collaboration package was introduced.

