- FoundationKit CI run `31257201388` — success;
  - release build/test/publish/pack path — success;
  - Workbench SQL integration — success;
  - Athar SQL/E2E + backup restore regression — success;
  - Madar SQL Server integration and end-to-end workflow — success;
- FoundationKit Security Scan run `31257201363` — success;
- FoundationKit CodeQL run `31257201368` — success.

The Madar SQL smoke path proves:

`create case → assign operator → operator POST comment → GET comments → continue lifecycle → resolve → close → audit timeline → comment body absent from audit metadata → comments still readable after close`.

The reusable package artifact from this exact head was inspected and remains unchanged at:

- 17 `.nupkg` packages;
- 17 `.snupkg` symbol packages.

No new reusable package was added for the Madar-specific collaboration slice.

## Implementation notes from verification

Exact-head CI exposed and the branch fixed two EF Core translation issues in `CaseCommentStore`: entity filtering and deterministic ordering are now applied before/within SQL-translatable projection. The final exact head above is the one on which all CI, SQL E2E, security, and CodeQL evidence passed.

## Deliberately deferred

Private/internal note tiers, mentions/watchers/subscriptions, notifications, attachments/files, edit/delete/version history, rich text/HTML, reactions, moderation, organization hierarchy/multi-tenancy, advanced search/reporting, reusable collaboration extraction, and Production Approval remain outside this slice.

