## Summary

Completes the remaining P1.1 dual-mode relay acceptance criteria from #3 while preserving ARVREL's virtual-output-only safety boundary.

The audit also found and fixes a real Research Mode policy bypass where `smv.allowsTrip` could previously be satisfied by non-executable/comment text rather than a true trip gate.

## What changed

### Hardened policy gate
- strips comments before structural/policy checks while hashing the original source;
- requires a real executable `trip = ...` assignment;
- requires `smv.allowsTrip` as an explicit conjunctive term in every executable trip expression;
- rejects comment-only, misplaced, negated, compared-false, and OR-bypass forms;
- rejects forbidden host capabilities only when they are executable, not when shown in comments/examples.

### Deterministic typed DSL runtime
P1.1 runtime activation is intentionally restricted to `50P-1`, `51P`, `50N`, and `51N`.

The interpreter exposes only typed measurements, active protection settings, SMV trust booleans, deterministic arithmetic/boolean expressions, bounded timers/integrators, and IEC curve evaluation. It exposes no file, network, process, reflection, unmanaged, host-object, or dynamic-code capability.

Hard limits:
- 64 KiB source;
- 64 statements;
- 512 interpreter instructions/frame;
- 64 runtime variable slots;
- bounded timer duration.

### Same-frame standard/custom A/B
`ResearchProtectionEngine` keeps the existing native `ProtectionEngine` as the standard reference oracle and runs validated custom source in parallel on the exact same `MeasurementFrame` for:
- internal deterministic laboratory;
- live IEC 61850 Sampled Values;
- PCAP/PCAPNG replay.

Staged custom remains shadow-only. After explicit activation, only that element's virtual 50/51 result becomes authoritative; the native standard result continues as parallel shadow evidence.

The high-rate path caches the registry snapshot and execution plan by mutation generation, avoiding repeated audit/plan reconstruction on every SMV frame.

### Explicit Stage → Activate → Rollback lifecycle
- Stage creates an immutable SHA-256-addressed definition tied to the active settings fingerprint;
- Activate accepts only the exact staged source hash and exact staged settings fingerprint;
- changing protection settings clears staged/active custom runtime and requires restaging;
- only one custom definition per element can be active;
- Rollback restores the previous custom definition or native standard algorithm;
- algorithm changes atomically reset timer/integration state and the virtual trip latch.

### Evidence and UI
Evidence includes:
- source hash and content-derived version;
- settings fingerprint;
- author/activation note;
- standard/custom per-frame A/B result;
- activation state and process-session audit trail;
- `virtual-only` output boundary.

The desktop editor now exposes Compile, deterministic A/B test, Stage, Activate and Rollback. While a custom definition is active the relay UI persistently reports `CUSTOM ACTIVE · VIRTUAL ONLY`. Activation/rollback is also appended durably to `%LocalAppData%\ARVREL\algorithms\activation-audit.jsonl`.

P2 feeder elements `67P`, `67N`, `27`, `59`, and `59N` remain source-visible / shadow-only by design; this PR does not broaden the P1.1 execution surface beyond the four requested 50/51 elements.

## Safety boundary

No physical output path is added. Custom activation cannot emit GOOSE trip, MMS control, relay contact output, unmanaged I/O, or any physical trip. The host re-applies `SmvTrustState.AllowsTrip` independently of the DSL before any virtual trip request can be published.

## Regression coverage

Added coverage for:
- policy bypasses through comments, OR, negation and false comparison;
- generated 50/51 source compilation;
- typed setting/unit failures and sandbox limits;
- exact definite-time timer boundary without early operation;
- SMV trip-block enforcement;
- deterministic standard/custom divergence;
- exact-hash and settings-fingerprint activation;
- Stage/Activate/Rollback lifecycle and evidence identity;
- shadow not changing native output;
- active custom becoming authoritative only for its virtual element;
- rollback restoring native standard output;
- settings changes clearing active custom runtime.

